+ <p class="eyebrow">01 / What we built</p><h2 id="build-title">We made a lamp that responds.</h2>
+ <p>We wanted desk lighting to feel attentive without spoken commands. LuxoIII notices people, welcomes an open palm, and follows a finger across a virtual desk. We run the AI locally so the interaction does not depend on a cloud service.</p>
+ <div class="build-grid"><div><h3>We see and interpret.</h3><p>We process the USB camera on the Arduino UNO Q: face detection, palm detection, 21 hand landmarks, and our gesture classifier. We use short gesture holds to avoid reacting to every uncertain frame.</p></div><div><h3>We connect the real and digital.</h3><p>We host this app on the UNO Q. Your browser renders our full mechanical model, blends its expressions, and shows the camera beside it. Pointing moves the simulated desk light; an open palm brings its attention back to you.</p></div><div><h3>We control what works.</h3><p>We track the largest face with the physical swivel, limited to ±45°. We switch D7 fully on or off, without PWM, using fresh face and beam-angle checks. Our stepper joints are damaged, so full-arm movement is simulated in this demo.</p></div></div>
